... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Information Technology Act 2000, Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita 2023

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
IT Act Section 66D, IT Act Section 66E, BNS Section 308, BNS Section 318, BNSS Section 482

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
AI Deepfake, Cyber Extortion, Digital Impersonation, Forensic Data Recovery, Custodial Interrogation

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
Petitioner created synthetic AI deepfake video of bank executive to extort commercial cryptocurrency payments.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
Whether anticipatory bail can be granted where digital devices used for generative AI extortion remain unrecovered?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
Pre-arrest bail cannot be granted where digital forensics and neural network servers must be seized to trace extortion proceeds.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Anticipatory Bail Dismissed; AI deepfake extortion ring requires custodial forensic interrogation.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice G. Jayachandran
Madras High Court \(Principal Seat, Chennai\)
[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]
) Tj ET
